  *General information notice.* This book offers psychological insight, personal development guidance, and practical self-development exercises for general readers. It is not a substitute for individual assessment, diagnosis, or treatment by a qualified health professional. Readers who are experiencing persistent distress, or who are concerned about their mental health, substance use, or safety, are encouraged to consult a qualified professional. Where a chapter discusses suicide, self-harm, addiction, or crisis, the text directs the reader to immediate professional and emergency support.

  *Limits of general advice.* Every person's circumstances, culture, health history, and obligations differ. Exercises, worksheets, and self-assessments in this book and its appendices are educational tools. They are not tests, and they do not produce a diagnosis. Readers should adapt the material to their own situation and, where appropriate, work through it with a counsellor, therapist, physician, or trusted mentor.

  *Stories and illustrations.* All case stories, vignettes, dialogues, and composite characters in this book are original illustrative material created for teaching purposes. They are not depictions of identifiable individuals, and any resemblance to specific persons or events is coincidental. Where a story is presented, it is labelled as illustrative or composite.

  *Illustrations.* Diagrams were prepared for this edition. Photographs are AI-generated illustrative images created for this edition and are labelled as illustrative images. They do not depict identifiable real persons or specific events.

  *Cultural scope.* The book is written from a broadly international perspective with particular attention to African and Nigerian contexts, including the expectations placed on men within extended-family systems. Readers elsewhere are encouraged to translate the guidance into their own cultural setting.

  *Style.* British spelling is used throughout. Terms that may be unfamiliar to general readers are defined in the Glossary.

  Typeset in EB Garamond and Source Sans 3. Trim size 6 × 9 inches.
